Read docs/CRYPTO_V6_TOP200_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task. Doctrine recap: DESIGN FREEZE — zero visual redesign, same table/columns/cards/panel, row count is data not design. ONE SOURCE RULE: every rendered crypto price goes through livePrice(row, spotRow) — new coins inherit it, never add a second path. Truth rules verbatim: price gate (venue vs CG 3%, stables 1%), CG-id joins, honest '—' beats plausible numbers, no zeros-as-data, llama TVL id-anchored <$1M null CEX excluded. Curation objective: top-200 = highest-mcap CG coins passing venue test, exclusions listed with reasons in docs/CRYPTO_UNIVERSE.md; deep-rank coins without perps/TVL get '—' = Binance parity, hard bar is spot+technicals. Standing constraints: NO new serverless files (?view= branches in api/crypto/markets.ts only), vercel.json keeps "regions":["fra1"], keyless APIs only and curl-verify each new endpoint/param shape from prod before coding (especially CG ids= with 200 ids), no new npm deps, additive payloads, hunt every hardcoded 100-cap in markets.ts when scaling. Audit tooling: apps/market-ui/scripts/audit_crypto_coverage.mjs — rerun after every task, paste REAL numbers into the Progress log. Verify per task: market-ui typecheck 0 + vercel --prod (from repo root — apps/market-ui path breaks project link) + prod curl with real numbers. Flip the task to [x], append one Progress-log line, commit on roadmap/world-class (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). PERSISTENCE: never end the loop because of a usage/rate limit, 429, or overloaded error — on any such error stop consuming tokens, ScheduleWakeup at 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger and resume the same task from its last verified step (ledger + Progress log + CRYPTO_UNIVERSE.md + CRYPTO_COVERAGE_AUDIT.md are recovery state; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations); chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining, or a task blocked on something only the user can provide — then say exactly what's needed and still ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes if supplied.
